lisa-design:
- Scope agreed with the user: everything lives in workflows/smoke/; local-dev is not touched and its .env is never read. local-dev compose files and scripts were only a read-only reference.
- Orchestration is a bash script (smoke/run.sh, bash 3.2 compatible) rather than a Go cmd: it is linear docker/curl/jq glue with no branching rules worth unit-testing as Go. Its behaviour (settings validation, failure -> ps/logs/down, SMOKE_KEEP) is tested from Go with fake docker/curl in internal/ciworkflows/smoke_test.go.
- No credentials provided by anyone: postgres uses throwaway postgres/postgres (port not published); CCF_JWT_SECRET is openssl-generated per run; no JWT key file paths, so the API generates its RSA pair in memory; the admin user is created via the API CLI (`/api users add`, distroless image so `exec` of the binary), and the agent key via POST /api/admin/agents + /keys (same flow as local-dev register-agents.sh). Secrets are ::add-mask::ed on Actions; the key secret is never printed; `users add` output (it logs the password) is shown only on failure.
- Readiness/migration check = GET /api/health/ready 200 (API migrates before listening, AutoMigrate has no migrations table) plus a psql check that ccf_users/ccf_agents/ccf_agent_service_account_keys/ccf_agent_instances exist. No compose healthchecks on api/agent: distroless images have no shell/curl; the host polls instead.
- Agent check requires an instance in GET /api/admin/agents/{id}/instances with heartbeat-config-revision != null: that field is only set by an authenticated heartbeat, so it proves both registration (config report at startup) and heartbeat. Heartbeat cadence is 1/min at a random second, hence SMOKE_TIMEOUT default 180s. Agent < 0.9.0 has no instance reporting and fails this check (verified with 0.8.1) -- intended, since the API pair is 0.21.0.
- The agent is started only after its key exists (`up -d --no-deps agent`), so compose.yaml uses ${SMOKE_AGENT_CLIENT_ID:-} (empty allowed) while the image tags use :? (required).
- Workflow checks out this repo at job.workflow_sha (same "Check the tools ref" guard as preview/release-helm) so callers get smoke/ from the workflow's own commit; permissions contents: read only; no app token needed (public images).
- W3 plugin hook: check_plugin() no-op in run.sh plus TODO(W3) markers in agent-config.yml and stack-smoke.yml; the plugin check must run inside run.sh while the stack is up, not as a later workflow step.
